# Known Lumina codebase mirrors

In the pursuit of independence, Lumina attempts to be as well
balanced over baskets as can be. It's **current** (as of August, 2026)
main mirror (mirror that others are following) is the Radicle repository
at [`rad:z3KozhW4C7ykQoe65DX8yUUGEHcdA`](https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z3KozhW4C7ykQoe65DX8yUUGEHcdA/).

### Official mirrors

Official repositories that are welcoming your contributions in code or comment:

- [Radicle](https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z3KozhW4C7ykQoe65DX8yUUGEHcdA/)
- [Tangled (`knot.ollie.earth` knot)](https://tangled.org/did:plc:dlfsjwtiq5zklprcrmhjxlsq)
- [Codeberg](https://codeberg.org/strawmelonjuice/Lumina)

### Personal mirrors

Other, more personal mirrors are probably mostly for their respective owners, but may help you find the code even if
other options may fail.

- [Forgejo `forge.strawmelonjuice.com`](https://forge.strawmelonjuice.com/strawmelonjuice/Lumina) (you can request an
  account, but using official mirrors is preferred)

[Add your own](https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z3KozhW4C7ykQoe65DX8yUUGEHcdA/tree/docs-new/development/mirrors.dj)

## Where to contribute

Any of the official mirrors above accept pull requests or patches, with of course a slight preference to Radicle, for
ease of gitting, but use whichever you prefer!

For issues, remains the preferred mirror, though issues on Codeberg are just as welcome, and issues on Radicle too (the
reason is that creating issues on Radicle takes some more effort than you might find it to be worth)
